            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nurse Ellen so not a"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this recipe and have used salmon as well. Also put sauteed sweet yellow and red bell peppers on top of the fish while cooking in the foil which adds great flavor. Thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2007-06-05T09:17:07.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ltlvxn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious! I used a whole salmon fillet that served two of us, a whole lemon and a whole jalapeno (fresh). Followed the recipe exactly and it was gorgeous! The fillet was frozen so I put it in the oven on 375 for 30 minutes and it came out perfectly. The only thing I would change is that I would de-seed the jalapeno next time as I found it a little spicy!!",
            "datePublished": "2008-11-07T19:18:46.160Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lisandreasings"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I adjusted the recipe for 6 filets, which meant 2T of garlic salt--and that was clearly TOO MUCH! Also, because I used jarred jalapenos there was too strong of a jalapeno flavor, too (&amp; my husband loves hot stuff!), because of the peppers containing more liquid, which got into the fish too much. If I try it again I'll use half as much garlic salt, and add garlic powder &amp; use fresh jalapenos (as the recipe states).",
            "datePublished": "2005-08-28T19:15:30.247Z"
          },
          {
